=== Text #18 ===
> [Indones]ia - Eko Nugroho[ and "]Way[ang] Bocor"
[E]ko Nurgoho[ is] one[ of] Indonesia's most provocative young artists whose style is a unique mix of Indonesia's rich traditions and popular culture tinged with dark humor. Using a distinctive blend of high and low art, Nugroho' "Way[ang] Bocor"[ is] a contemporary form of theater in which puppets and actors weave together traditional elements of Indonesian 'wayag' (shadow puppets) with live theater and scripts that[ cast a] satir[ic] view of contemporary subjects. The show "God Bliss"[ tells] the story of how Islam[ came] to Java, and[ became] absorbed as part of[ J]avanese culture that includes elements of Hinduism, Buddhism, and animism. Simultaneously playful and penetrating.[]

